# Documentation

Canonical docs live under `docs/` plus root `README.md`.

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `README.md` | Overview, ports, credentials, commands |
| `docs/guides/INSTALLATION.md` | Setup, env, migrate, seed, Docker |
| `docs/guides/COMPETITION_OPS.md` | Day-of ops by role |
| `docs/api/API.md` | `/api/v1` overview |
| `docs/architecture/OVERVIEW.md` | Layers, scoring isolation, sockets |
| `docs/architecture/ER_DIAGRAM.md` | Entity relationships |

## Rules

- Update the relevant existing doc when behavior/ports/env/API contracts change — don’t create parallel guides.
- Keep seed credentials and ports in sync with `.env.example` and README.
- Document permission names and publish/approval flows accurately.
- Prefer linking to Swagger (`/api/docs`) for exhaustive endpoint lists; keep `API.md` as the narrative map.
- Cursor rules (`.cursor/rules/`) are agent guidance — not a substitute for user-facing docs.
